## Insertion Sort

### 📌 Problem Description
Implement the Insertion Sort algorithm to sort an array of integers in ascending order by building a sorted portion of the array one element at a time.

### 💡 Approach
1. Start from the second element of the array, considering the first element as already sorted.
2. Store the current element as the `key`.
3. Compare the key with the elements in the sorted portion, moving from right to left.
4. Shift all elements greater than the key one position to the right.
5. Insert the key into its correct position.
6. Repeat until the entire array is sorted.

### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis
- **Best Case:** O(n) — when the array is already sorted.
- **Average Case:** O(n²)
- **Worst Case:** O(n²) — when the array is sorted in reverse order.
- **Space Complexity:** O(1) — sorting is performed in place.

### 🛠️ Language
Java

###Solution

class Solution {
    public int[] insertionSort(int[] nums) {
        // Iterate from the second element up to the end of the array
        for (int i = 1; i < nums.length; i++) {
            int key = nums[i];
            int j = i - 1;

            // Shift elements of nums[0..i-1] that are greater than key
            // to one position ahead of their current position
            while (j >= 0 && nums[j] > key) {
                nums[j + 1] = nums[j];
                j--;
            }
            // Place the key at its correct sorted position
            nums[j + 1] = key;
        }
        return nums;
    }
}
